    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260921\">@Julia Markus Himmel</span> As far as I see <code>Std.HashSet.mem_toList</code> is the only lemma available for hashsets while hashmaps have more lemmas available. This is problematic as it requires LawfulBEq.  Should this be extended?</p>",
        "id": 606184798,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1782290468
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Std.HashSet.contains_toList#doc\">docs#Std.HashSet.contains_toList</a> should be useful.</p>",
        "id": 606194292,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1782293263
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't see directly how this helps. Something along <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Std.HashMap.mem_toList_iff_getKey%3F_eq_some_and_getElem%3F_eq_some#doc\">docs#Std.HashMap.mem_toList_iff_getKey?_eq_some_and_getElem?_eq_some</a> would be useful</p>",
        "id": 606197286,
        "sender_full_name": "Johannes Tantow",
        "timestamp": 1782294216
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well at least it characterizes <code>toList</code> without requiring <code>LawfulBEq</code>...</p>",
        "id": 606200149,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1782295115
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually you're right that isn't quite enough</p>",
        "id": 606202404,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1782295727
    },
    {
